  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 229 PM EDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nGenerally quiet weather is expected for the first half of the long \nterm with a dry airmass in place. We'll also get a break from \nthunderstorms during the afternoon as well until Wednesday when \nwinds become more southerly and we start to pull moisture back in \nfrom the Gulf.\n\nAfter Wednesday, a trough in the upper level flow will bring back \nthe chances for afternoon thunderstorms. The most potent upper level \ndynamics will remain north of us, as the center of the low will \nremain in the Great Lakes region. Given slowly increasing \ntemperatures however, we won't lack instability during the \nafternoon. This pattern will remain in place through the weekend.",
